{
  "_about": "Every crash the fuzzers found outside our typed errors (Addendum L, L-T10). `status` open = a patch is with the owner (lane3/hooks/L-T10/) and the strict test named in `test` is an expected failure while the id is in the test file's OPEN / KNOWN_OPEN dict (it shows as an UNEXPECTED SUCCESS when the owner applies the patch: delete the id and set `status` to fixed); fixed = the id is gone and the test is an ordinary one. tests/test_fuzz_regressions.py replays every entry: `call` names the route (the target function and its typed-error policy), `input` is what is sent (a JSON value, {\"base64\": ...} for bytes, {\"repeat\": [[piece, count], ...]} for a long text), `more_inputs` are extra cases; an entry whose input is too big to store has `synthetic` (what the named test builds) and is replayed by that test. `only_on` (\"nt\") marks a finding that exists only on Windows: its replay is an expected failure there while open, an ordinary test elsewhere.",
